  "verbalization": "Dexamethasone, a corticosteroid, is implicated in the pathogenesis of Rosacea through a chain of indications that ultimately lead to the disease. The evidence suggests that Dexamethasone is associated with Iris Disease and Panuveitis, both of which are linked to Medrysone, a corticosteroid with a known role in Rosacea. This indicates a potential mechanistic pathway where corticosteroids may contribute to the development of Rosacea by modulating inflammatory processes or affecting ocular structures. The indirect relationship through Medrysone supports the idea that corticosteroids could play a role in the pathophysiology of Rosacea, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple indirect pathways, including the use of Loteprednol Etabonate as a related corticosteroid, further reinforces the hypothesis that corticosteroids may influence disease progression in Rosacea through inflammatory or structural mechanisms.",
